From a7c5d5202445d6351bf15606ace3fda870435e27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:13:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: owner cards are created with the
 judged text; replayed couriers reuse their landing

Review t_01a1ced25af29218: relay-time owner verdicts judge the hub's own local-owner text (shared builder) and store it on the route, so the probe creates exactly that card; a stored verdict runs the judge's full validation and a failed check is a final deny, not a retry; only a hub home is judged at relay time, the verdict event is recorded where the owner lands, and an owner sent to the hub is judged by the hub's own create; a re-applied courier request reuses its stored placement (no second judge, no conflict); the hub CLI receive path judges without the origin's placement note; the unreachable placement_policy branch is gone.
